A few notes on wiring this into a real app:
- `onBack` should pop your in-app route stack (not browser history) — `BackButton`'s click only fires your callback, it doesn't navigate anything itself.
- `onPay` should throw on failure so the MainButton's progress state clears and `submitError` shows; on success, route away from checkout (and the form will naturally stop being "dirty").
- The fallback back-button only appears when `Telegram.WebApp` isn't present, so you can still use/test this component in a plain browser without producing two back controls inside the actual Mini App.
